description: Implement already-written RegImpact specs as code (no interview, no new product spec).
alwaysApply: false
---

When the user wants the product built from the written specs, follow
`.cursor/skills/implement-spec/SKILL.md` the way Apple design reviews follow that skill.

- Do not interview. Do not write a new product spec. Do not wait for approval.
- Implement `spec/01`–`spec/17` one MVP stage at a time. Default: first incomplete stage.
- Start coding in the same turn. Progress logs go in `spec/impl/` only.
- Verify with `pytest` and `ruff check .` when the environment can. Do not commit unless asked.
- Follow the spec only. No extra features. No SQLite or fake Bedrock. Missing Docker or AWS is not a stop — write the spec code and list installs at the end.

Trigger when the user asks to implement the specs, start coding, build the MVP, build a stage,
continue implementation, or make the app from the specs.
